      "graphs": [
        {
          "candidate_id": "g0",
          "components": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "quote": "I think it is reasonable that a debt not be deemed \"verified\" or \"substantiated\" unless and until there's a final non-appealable order",
              "occurrence": 0,
              "type": "policy"
            },
            {
              "id": "c2",
              "quote": "if you dispute a debt, the debt collector reports you to the CRAs  and your credit standing is adversely impacted",
              "occurrence": 0,
              "type": "fact"
            },
            {
              "id": "c3",
              "quote": "the notation on the credit report that the debt is disputed by the consumer is largely ignored by potential lenders, employers, landlords, etc.",
              "occurrence": 0,
              "type": "fact"
            },
            {
              "id": "c4",
              "quote": "The debt collector and creditor threaten to report you to the CRAs as a coercive tactic to force you to pay a debt",
              "occurrence": 0,
              "type": "fact"
            },
            {
              "id": "c5",
              "quote": "This proposal would also protect consumers from having their credit standing negatively impacted until after it is conclusively determined that a purported debt that is disputed is in fact owed",
              "occurrence": 0,
              "type": "policy"
            },
            {
              "id": "c6",
              "quote": "a rule could be adopted that would impose significant statutory penalties, treble damanages and recovery of attorney's fees",
              "occurrence": 0,
              "type": "policy"
            },
            {
              "id": "c7",
              "quote": "the burden of proof should be on the creditors and debt collectors to affirmatively prove the existence and amount of any disputed debt before a consumer's credit report is adversely impacted.",
